# esp32s3-aitrip-480x480 -- AITRIP / Guition ESP32-4848S040, ESP32-S3 N16R8, 4.0in 480x480 RGB panel.
# Derived from esp32s3-n8r2.manifest minus hardware this board does not carry:
#   Sonar, PCA9685, WS2812, LCD1602 -- none are fitted.
# NO PANEL FILES YET.  [P231] phase 0 extracted the ST7789 (a PUSH panel) behind LL_Panel; the
# ST7701S path this board needs (16-bit RGB SCAN *plus* a 3-wire SPI init handshake) does not
# exist.  Staging lcd-* here before that driver exists would ship a callable no-op.
# esp32s3-n8r2 — same as esp32-s3-devkitc-1.
#
# esp32s3-n8r2-00.manifest and -01.manifest are SYMLINKS to this file: two physical N8R2
# units, one ship-list, so they cannot drift apart.  They are separate ENVS only so a flash
# and a result bind to one board (see w3_ai_scripts/board_macs.tsv).  An env with no manifest
# stages no data_staged/<env>/, and uploadfs then dies with
#   Building FS image from 'data' directory ... warning: can't read source directory
# which reads as a filesystem problem, not a missing manifest.  If the units ever need
# different files, replace the symlink -- do not copy this file and edit one.

# Core runtime
core/setup.scm
core/Compiler.scm
core/Lobs.scm
core/Behaviors.scm
core/Terminal.scm
file: boards/pins/esp32s3-n8r2.scm -> Pins.scm
core/Timers.scm
core/ESP32.scm
core/CommonIO.scm
core/Buzzer.scm
core/WiFi.scm
core/I2C.scm
