# Dev tools
tools/llip-server.scm
# LLIP serial receiver -- setup.scm loads it when present (see core/setup.scm).
# NOTE ON WHAT A MANIFEST DECIDES: every target already RECEIVES all of the Scheme library --
# w3_make_release_one copies the whole scm/ tree into every package (w3_make.sh ~line 354).
# A manifest only chooses the DEFAULT on-device FS subset; anything omitted is still shipped
# and can be staged or loaded at runtime.  This file is listed because it must be RESIDENT AT
# BOOT to be useful: without it in the FS the board cannot accept `llip --serial PORT send`,
# so pushing one settings file costs a full filesystem upload through pio -- which also wipes
# .pio/build for every other env and forces concurrent sessions to rebuild.
features/llip-serial.scm

tools/test-framework.scm

# Board-specific init
boards/esp32s3-n8r2.scm
# Target setup: paints a boot banner so a running panel is distinguishable FROM THE FRONT.
# Without it a healthy board and a dead one are both just black -- and the only other way to ask
# is a serial port, which resets this board.  See the file's header.
boards/setup-esp32s3-aitrip-480x480.scm

# Runtime defaults
runtime-defaults/Settings.scm
# Peer CA for the `network` test_id: written by _w3_run_network, absent otherwise (untracked).
optional: runtime-defaults/net-test-ca.pem -> net-test-ca.pem
# [P69] LLIP auth test key pair for llip-auth-tests.scm: written by w3_ai_scripts/llip_test_keys.sh,
# absent otherwise (untracked, and deliberately so -- see that script's header).
optional: runtime-defaults/llip-test-privkey.scm -> llip-test-privkey.scm
optional: runtime-defaults/llip-test-pubkey.scm -> llip-test-pubkey.scm
# Bench WiFi credentials: untracked, absent by default, silent when absent (see .example).
optional: runtime-defaults/Settings-local.scm.hud -> Settings-local.scm

# PER-TARGET SETTINGS OVERLAY -- setup.scm's THIRD settings layer, merged ahead of the two above
# so these keys win and everything unmentioned is inherited.  REQUIRED, not `optional:`, because
# unlike Settings-local.scm this file is TRACKED: it is present in every checkout, so its absence
# is a fault and should say so rather than pass silently.
# It carries NO CREDENTIALS -- scm/ ships wholesale to public repos.  SSID and password belong in
# the Settings-local.scm.* layer, which .gitignore covers and _w3_release_scrub deletes outright.
file: runtime-defaults/Settings-env.panel.scm -> Settings-env.scm
runtime-defaults/Settings-Lamb.scm

# Test suite
# Perf/gcpause bench files only (small).  The correctness tiers (smoke/conform/subsystem/extend)
# are delivered INCREMENTALLY per-tier by _w3_run_correct_esp32 -- the full ~460KB ll_tests suite
# is NOT shipped to embedded FS.
file: tests/ll_tests/bench-runner.scm   -> ll_tests/bench-runner.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/benchmarks.scm     -> ll_tests/benchmarks.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/bignum-hw-probe.scm -> ll_tests/bignum-hw-probe.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/bignum-hw-sweep.scm      -> ll_tests/bignum-hw-sweep.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/bignum-cost-probe.scm   -> ll_tests/bignum-cost-probe.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/bignum-hw-cliff.scm     -> ll_tests/bignum-hw-cliff.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/gc-pause-bench.scm -> ll_tests/gc-pause-bench.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/pause_bench.scm    -> ll_tests/pause_bench.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/ncg-fusion-probe.scm -> ll_tests/ncg-fusion-probe.scm

# [P123] Part G -- the mini-HUD: camera frames from the 4WD, metrics around them.
# llip-vision is Part D's BINARY frame codec (s-expression header + raw bytes, no base64) and is
# already in the 4WD's manifest -- the SENDER half has shipped there since 2026-09-17.  This panel
# only needs the same codec to read it, plus the sink that puts a frame on the glass instead of in
# a file, which is the one thing Part D did not have (its consumer is a VLM, which takes a path).
features/llip-vision.scm
# The three-layer display stack: a thin 1:1 shim over LVGL lives in C++; these two are the
# layers above it.  Widgets compose shim calls into a readout or a gauge; the layout decides
# which exist, where they sit and what they mean.  Both push over LLIP in seconds, so an
# arrangement can be changed without a rebuild.
# NTP.  The HUD shows a wall clock to the second, and a board with no time source shows dashes --
# correct, but useless.  nettime-sync! fetches over NTP and sets the system clock.
features/nettime.scm
# A board that will not associate is diagnosed by comparing the SSID it is configured for against
# what its OWN antenna can hear -- a scan from a workstation answers neither, because this panel's
# display bus costs it 10-13 dB.  (net-why) does that cross-reference on the board and says which
# of the three cases it is.  It must be RESIDENT rather than typed: the serial console echoes every
# character, so a hand-typed scan loop returns kilobytes of echo wrapped around the answer.
features/netscan.scm

features/lvgl-widgets.scm
demos/hud-layout.scm
demos/hud-panel.scm

# PANEL COLOUR-CAPABILITY DIAGNOSTIC.  Not loaded at boot -- `(load "panel-colortest.scm")` when
# you need it.  It draws with `lcd-box` straight into the framebuffer, so running it REPLACES
# whatever the HUD is showing; that is intended, and a reboot or a panel restart brings the HUD
# back.  It exists because the "red and blue quantise in steps of 8" claim in the tree is read off
# a schematic and has never been measured, and because the predicted symptom of that defect is
# indistinguishable from ordinary RGB565 quantisation on a correctly wired panel.
demos/panel-colortest.scm
